DDLC Control Centre
====================

Verified game package
---------------------

The supplied `ddlc-win.zip` is an intact DDLC 1.1.1 desktop package. Its
`game/scripts.rpa` uses RPA-3.0 and contains compiled Ren'Py scripts. The bundled
runtime metadata reports Ren'Py 6.99.12.3. The package includes `DDLC.exe`,
`DDLC.sh`, Windows 32-bit runtime files, and Linux x86_64/i686 runtime files.
It is not a browser port and cannot be launched as an ordinary web page.

The verified Act entry labels are `ch0_main`, `ch21_main`, `ch30_main`, and
`ch40_main`. The patch also checks every requested scene against
`renpy.get_all_labels()`/`renpy.has_label()` at runtime. The bridge rejects
navigation targets that the connected game has not advertised. Direct jumps
can still change game state or story flow; use them only when appropriate.

Private installation
--------------------

Keep the original ZIP in the repository root as `ddlc-win.zip` or set
`DDLC_ARCHIVE` to its path. It is ignored by Git. Install once with:

    python3 bridge.py --install-recommended

The installer validates ZIP paths and required files, extracts to
`private-game/DDLC-1.1.1-pc/`, and copies `ddlc_control_centre.rpy` into that
private game's `game/` directory. It refuses to overwrite an existing install.
The extracted game and local ZIP are ignored by Git and must not be committed or
published. `DDLC_GAME_DIR` can select a different install directory.

Run the local bridge on the same computer and user account as the game:

    python3 bridge.py

Open the bridge's forwarded port 8765 in Codespaces. Keep its visibility
private. The bridge serves the app and API on one origin. It creates a
0600-permission random token at `~/.ddlc-control-centre-token`; the browser page
receives the token from the local server, and the Ren'Py patch reads the same
file. The bridge binds only to 127.0.0.1 and checks browser origins.

Opening the HTML directly with `file://` leaves browser-only terminal and ZIP
inspection controls available, but bridge, native launch, and live game
commands are unavailable. The UI reports this instead of waiting on requests.

Recommended launch and device limits
------------------------------------

Run Recommended Version inspects the configured local installation and only
starts its native launcher when required files, the installed patch, a
supported host runtime, and a graphical session are available. A process start
is reported as a launch request; the UI reports the game as connected only
after the Ren'Py patch polls the bridge.

The current Codespace has the game files and patch installed, but no graphical
display. It can inspect files and run the web preview; it cannot show the
native DDLC window. A browser on an iPad or Chromebook cannot execute a Windows
`.exe`, display a desktop process running on another computer, or reach a
bridge bound to that other device's localhost. For native gameplay, run the
bridge and private game installation on the same graphical desktop. The
supplied archive has no native macOS runtime.

Upload Custom inspects ZIP contents without changing the selected archive.
Only a browser package with a detected HTML entry point can be previewed in the
sandboxed iframe. `run <filename>` only opens that supported HTML entry point;
`.exe`, `.sh`, `.rpa`, scripts, and other files are not treated as executable.
Custom desktop games require separate manual installation and a compatible
local runtime. The required custom-upload warning is shown in the launcher.

Ren'Py patch
------------

For another local installation, copy `ddlc_control_centre.rpy` into its
`game/` directory and start `bridge.py` under the same OS user. The patch polls
`/poll`, reports runtime labels through `/result`, checks labels with
`renpy.has_label`, and performs jumps outside its network exception handler so
Ren'Py control-flow exceptions are not swallowed. The draggable in-game CC
button is an overlay and does not request a window resize or exit fullscreen.

Tests and troubleshooting
-------------------------

Run the available checks with:

    python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v
    node --test tests/test_control_centre*.js

- Missing game files: place the private ZIP at `ddlc-win.zip`, then run the
  installer. An existing destination is never replaced automatically.
- Bridge token errors: run the bridge and game as the same user; confirm
  `~/.ddlc-control-centre-token` is readable by that user.
- Game remains disconnected: verify the patch exists at
  `private-game/DDLC-1.1.1-pc/game/ddlc_control_centre.rpy` and that the game
  can reach `127.0.0.1:8765` on the same host.
- Desktop launch unavailable: use a graphical desktop with the matching
  bundled runtime. A headless Codespace or remote tablet browser cannot display
  the host desktop game.
- Scene or Act rejected: run `scene list` while the patch is connected; only
  labels reported by that running game are enabled.
- Browser archive rejected: ZIP64, encrypted entries, unsafe paths, symlinks,
  archives over 512 MiB, and extracted packages over 1 GiB are unsupported.
